    {
      "id": "chase-sapphire-dining",
      "title": "Dining Loyalty, from Scratch.",
      "description": [
        "Chase had no dining loyalty program, even as competitors offered cardholders dedicated dining perks and discovery tools. Sapphire Reserve holders already had a $300 annual dining credit sitting largely unused, with nothing built to help them find where to spend it — a gap the Sapphire team wanted closed, with reservations handled through a network partner rather than built in-house."
      ],
      "description2": [
        "As sole product designer, I mapped an 18-month vision — rich visuals, ratings, and content pulled from partners like Infatuation — then shipped a lean MVP to test demand, connecting Sapphire holders to exclusive, cardholder-only tables through OpenTable. It became the second-most-used Sapphire Reserve benefit within four months."
      ],
      "metadata": [
        {
          "icon": "person",
          "text": "Sole Product Designer"
        },
        {
          "icon": "bolt",
          "text": "0–1 Product Design"
        },
        {
          "icon": "chart",
          "text": "3M users, second-most-used Sapphire benefit in 4 months. Scaled from 30 to 60 cities in 2 months"
        }
      ],
